    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0143" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg39"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 26,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Blaine informs Mr. Mizner that the Department’s instructions to him appear to
                    have been intercepted, urgent protests against the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Colima</hi> seizure remaining unacknowledged. He adds that this is the
                    seventh telegraphic message sent to the legation at Guatemala City since the
                    19th instant, and instructs him to demand an immediate investigation and
                    inviolability of his official correspondence; remarking the similarity between
                    the present situation and that of 1885, when Mr. Hall’s telegraphic
                    communications were cut.</p>
            </div>
